## Test Anti-Pattern Audit — Severity-Ranked Findings

This test suite is a textbook example of **"coverage without verification"** — every production method is invoked (achieving line coverage) but almost nothing meaningful is asserted.

---

### 🔴 Critical — Tests That Prove Nothing

#### 1. Missing outcome assertions (all tests)

**Pattern:** Call a method, never verify the result or side-effect.

| Test | What's missing |
|------|---------------|
| `AddProduct_Works` (L19-21) | No assert at all. Doesn't verify the product was stored. |
| `UpdatePrice_Works` (L34-35) | Calls `UpdatePrice` but never checks the new price persisted. |
| `RemoveProduct_Works` (L39-41) | Never asserts `GetProduct` returns `null` afterward. |
| `GetProductCount_Works` (L64-66) | Captures `count` in a local variable — never asserts its value. |
| `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` (L69-74) | Applies 10% discount but never checks resulting prices. |
| `ImportFromCsv_Works` (L85-88) | Imports data, never verifies any product exists afterward. |

**Fix pattern:**
```csharp
// AddProduct_Works → 
_catalog.AddProduct(product);
var stored = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, stored!.Price);
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", stored.Name);

// UpdatePrice_Works →
_catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);
Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001")!.Price);

// RemoveProduct_Works →
_catalog.RemoveProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNull(_catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001"));

// GetProductCount_Works →
_catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
Assert.AreEqual(1, _catalog.GetProductCount());

// ApplyBulkDiscount_Works →
_catalog.ApplyBulkDiscount(0.10m);
Assert.AreEqual(8.991m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001")!.Price);

// ImportFromCsv_Works →
_catalog.ImportFromCsv("SKU-001,Widget,9.99");
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001")!.Name);
```

---

### 🟠 High — Weak Assertions That Always Pass

#### 2. `Assert.IsNotNull` on non-nullable collections (L51, L59)

`Search` and `GetAll` return `List<Product>` — they **never** return null. The assert is vacuous.

**Fix:**
```csharp
// SearchProducts_Works →
var results = _catalog.Search("Widget");
Assert.AreEqual(1, results.Count);
